{"name":"Fried Egg","hex":"#ffe464","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fried egg","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An egg that has been shallow-fried on one or both sides without being beaten or stirred.","A golf ball half-buried in sand in a bunker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fried_egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fried egg","blocks":[{"text":"A fried egg is a dish made from one or more eggs which are removed from their shells, placed into a frying pan and cooked. They are traditionally eaten for breakfast or brunch in many countries but may also be served at other times of the day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Fried_Egg_2.jpg/330px-Fried_Egg_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fried_egg","wikidata":"Q274151"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg","wikidata":"Q17147"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Pecena_jaja1.jpg/500px-Pecena_jaja1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Pecena_jaja1.jpg/1280px-Pecena_jaja1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e